WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
this past week it's been revealed that  t1 ceo joe marsh and several other t1  employees were part of a private t1 fan  discord server many t1 fans have been  outraged to find out that not only were  marsh and other t1 employees sharing  exclusive and behind the scenes content  there for free but that he also made  personal and crew jokes about one of the  team's players there there's even been  an accusation that he failed to act on a  racist remark left in the server by one  of the users it's an incredibly strange  story all round let's get into it  okay we're going to be doing a deep dive  today into a secret discord so while  you're buckling up for that just make  sure you're subscribed to the channel  and if you enjoyed the video at the end  make sure you leave a like on your way  out the door we really do appreciate it  okay so we all know t1 the most  successful org in league's history the  home of faker and probably the team i've  talked about most on this channel other  than tsm in march of this year t1  launched their global fan platform  powered by b stage the idea was that  this platform would give t1 fans a more  intimate way to engage with the players  especially after two years of a pandemic  that meant they couldn't really see them  in person the platform offers fans  exclusive content including behind the  scenes videos and even the chance to  directly communicate with the players at  the time invent global quoted t1 ceo joe  marsh as saying quote the competitive  edge and legacy of t1 is all thanks to  the support and love from fans i am very  excited that the new platform and  membership will allow for the players  and fans to feel a bit closer now for  the sake of this story it's important to  remember here that this is all a paid  subscription t1 are offering behind the  scenes content but only if you fork out  the cash for it and as far as i'm aware  this system seemed to work well on the  surface until last weekend when all hell  broke loose the korean outlet never  reported that t1 ceo joe marsh have been  sharing daily behind the scenes pictures  of the players to a private discord  called t1 happy house for overseas fans  reportedly the fans who were paying 70  000 won or roughly 53 us dollars for  their t1 memberships for all that  exclusive behind the scenes content were  not happy about this it sounded a lot  like what they were paying for was being  given to others mainly western fans for  absolutely free on top of that the  article also outlined an alleged case of  racism in the discord server as well  some of you may remember the recent t1  protest trucks that angry fans have been  sending to t1 games in protest of their  management well allegedly one user  reacted to that in the discord server by  suggesting that quote we will put kimchi  in the truck invin global's ashley kang  outlined the controversy further on  twitter she shared images allegedly from  the discord which appeared to show merch  leaks from ceo joe marsh as well as  details of contract negotiations with  players agents and behind the scenes  pictures of the players there was also a  conversation which allegedly showed joe  marsh discussing a player photo shoot  with fans in which he asked who was  going to spray oil on their jungler  owner which he later described as a  thirst trap so this was pretty crazy  news not only did it look like t1  membership subscribers were missing out  on exclusive content being given to  others for completely free but the  discord server in which that content was  being shared in was being accused of  containing at least one racist comment  from a user and a conversation in which  t1 ceo joked about covering a player in  oil as a thirst trap kang also shared a  message allegedly sent to t1 membership  subscribers by t1 in which they  apologize for the situation specifically  they mentioned the sharing of photos and  information on an unofficial discord  channel and the fact that the discord  communications were conducted in only  one language they resolved to not make  the same mistake in future said that all  t1 members had now left the discord and  pledged that those with t1 membership  will receive more and better exclusive  content moving forward this message was  not a public statement from t1 and  pressure began to mount earlier this  week for there to be a more official  addressing of the situation on monday  joe marsh did just that he shared a twit  longer in which he began by apologizing  from the bottom of his heart for what he  called a confusing and disappointing  turn of events he admitted that he and  several other t1 employees were involved  in the discord server and asked for  forgiveness he explained how he and  other t1 employees disclosed sensitive  information and posted pictures that  originated internally marsh claimed he  thought these pictures would be okay for  him to post because they were not going  to be used anywhere else but admitted  this was wrong and that it undermined  the trust of the t1 fan membership he  also acknowledged that he made  inappropriate jokes about owner on the  discord server including the joke about  covering him with oil as a thirst trap  marsh added that he has apologized to  owner directly for this and that he will  make sure nothing like this ever happens  again now at this point on the twit  longer we reached something that wasn't  touched on at all in the t1 membership  message shared by ashley kang on twitter  the allegations of racist remarks on the  discord server marsh said he had been  made aware of racist remarks in the  server and admitted that neither he nor  other t1 employees filed a complaint or  took action he stressed that if he had  known about it at the time then he would  have done something but acknowledged  that wasn't an excuse that he should  have been more mindful given a similar  past incident and that it was a clear  mistake to not realize what was going on  finally marsh admitted that it was wrong  for him to remain on the server as for  the future he announced his decision to  take a six-month salary cut to never  talk about the team's personal details  on any channels and that t1 employees  who are on the server will be sent to a  disciplinary committee many of the top  replies in korean to marsha's tweet were  less than positive some describe trust  as being shattered said they were  disappointed and urged the ceo to  disclose the relevant staff involved in  the discord server but it's unclear  whether we'll hear any more on this  matter marsha's statement seem pretty  final and i'm sure that both he and t1  will not want to draw any more attention  at this time for those of you that have  been following t1 haven't been going  through the easiest of times this year  on the rift their record-breaking  perfect regular season in spring and  their second place finish at msi would  be enviable to any other team but  outside of the game there's been a lot  of friction between them and some  elements of their fanbase in july we  spoke about how faker is suing his toxic  fans who have sent him images and videos  described by his legal team as  unspeakably foul and just last week we  saw the return of the protest trucks  being sent to t1 games with messages  calling out t1 for what some fans see as  bad management from the team's coaches  and this all comes at a time when joe  marsh has recently spoken about t1 fans  getting way too close to players in  public even to the point of stalking  protesting in korea is a way of life and  part of the culture i don't mind the  protests what i mind is fans lingering  in the alley and popping out at my guys  when they're walking home and like  trying to get pictures with them or  lingering outside our building like  that's not cool like the trucks whatever  they are what they are like i'd rather  have trucks than no fans but  the stalking my players and like ruining  their lives and having them be afraid to  go to the movies because they're worried  that they don't practice too much  because they've had 18 hours of scrims  and like they can't have a social life  like that's draining on my guys more  than like a couple trucks the last thing  joe marsh mentioned in his twitter  longer about the discord server was that  he especially wanted to apologize to t1  players and staff as they prepare for  summer playoffs and a potential world's  run this year and we're not even done  with it yet has seen more headlines for  t1 than some other teams see in years  both good and bad they have an extremely  talented team of four up-and-comers  assisted by the veteran of veterans  himself in faker they have a good shot  of returning to the top in a way we've  not seen from this team in years but to  truly realize that potential i'm sure  that everyone at t1 will want to keep  any friction with fans and controversies  like this weeks to an absolute minimum  [Music]  you

